From 217bed70c3276a47effd5a80d70a4b646bfb62e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] soc: apple: add opt-in A9 AOP active driver and IIO
 accelerometer

Add a default-off driver (CONFIG_APPLE_A9_AOP_ACTIVE, plus the immutable
boot parameter apple_a9_aop.active=1) that boots the J71t AOP and exposes
its accelerometer through IIO. The passive observer is unchanged except
for an accessor for its debug parameter.

- Refuses unless all five AOP PMGR domains are on; never forces a domain,
  never clears mailbox faults, never resets the AOP. A running AOP with an
  empty outbox is refused; with pending words the first must be HELLO.
- Cold load: the image goes to the AOP region at IOP 0x01000000, the ext
  segment to a DRAM buffer whose address goes into the EC0p tag, the tags
  iOS writes (AOPt, nCal, WrAd, McRA, SOC_, SOCR, DEVf, STKG, PRNG, RTTO)
  are patched, then remap, mailbox masks, outbox enable and CPU release as
  AppleA7IOPV2 does.
- Own codec for the A7IOPV2 64-bit FIFO (endpoint in bits 63:56): Linux
  RTKit carries the endpoint in a separate word and its management type
  field overlaps this endpoint byte, so it cannot be reused.
- RTBuddy management: HELLO 12, EPMAP replies, AP power, IOP power state
  0x20, STARTEP for application endpoints, 1 s ping with a 5 s timeout.
- SPU/AFK v8: waits for the device's 0x80, answers 0xa0, allocates 0x89
  buffers with dma_alloc_coherent (48-bit physical reply), checks the
  AOP-written v7 ring headers, sends 0xa3, reads rings on 0x85 and writes
  commands with the channel in the entry and a conditional 0xa2 doorbell.
- Binds the "accel" ready report, sends the optional per-device
  calibration file, sets 100 ms batch/report intervals with a reply check
  per property, and registers IIO after the first 0xc2 report: raw counts,
  16.16 g scale, read-only 10 Hz, DT mount matrix and a triggered buffer
  fed by the device's own trigger.
- Shutdown/kexec stops the stream and sends AFK shutdown to every
  endpoint so the AOP stops writing to memory the next kernel reuses.
- Root-only debugfs (with apple_a9_aop.debug=1): state, mailbox
  transcript, ring dumps and the patched tag table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
